From 283e01b80cc64bbf89b99413f3390b7d63d05e76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yonglunyao <yonglunyao@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:40:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] platform/arm64: import huawei-gaokun-ec driver stack from
 mainline v7.2-rc2

Import the Huawei Matebook E Go (gaokun3, SC8280XP) embedded controller
driver stack verbatim from torvalds/linux v7.2-rc2, the exact base the
linux-gaokun-buildbot CI applies its EC patch series onto:

  - drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c    (EC core, blob 80a8ba8b)
  - drivers/power/supply/huawei-gaokun-battery.c (battery/adapter, blob e4dfec3b)
  - drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c  (UCSI, not yet 6.6-compatible)
  - include/linux/platform_data/huawei-gaokun-ec.h

6.6 has no drivers/platform/arm64/ yet, so create the directory with a
minimal Kconfig/Makefile (menuconfig ARM64_PLATFORM_DEVICES +
EC_HUAWEI_GAOKUN, as in mainline) and hook it into drivers/platform/.
Wire BATTERY_HUAWEI_GAOKUN and UCSI_HUAWEI_GAOKUN likewise; the UCSI
entry drops the "select DRM_AUX_HPD_BRIDGE" which does not exist in 6.6.

The buildbot's 4 EC patches (upstream 0012/0015/0016, others 0017) are
absorbed as follow-up commits.

Original driver by Pengyu Luo <mitltlatltl@gmail.com>.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: yonglunyao <yonglunyao@gmail.com>
